### MS6 Reputation - requetes de test (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
@host = http://localhost:8086
@dev = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### Contrat : reputation d'un developpeur
GET {{host}}/api/developers/{{dev}}/reputation

### Contrat : badges
GET {{host}}/api/developers/{{dev}}/badges

### Contrat : classement (filtrable par competence)
GET {{host}}/api/rankings?skill=java&page=0&size=20

### Contrat : ingestion d'evenement (202 APPLIED, puis DUPLICATE_IGNORED si renvoye)
POST {{host}}/api/reputation/events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "CHALLENGE_WON", "developerId": "33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333",
  "challengeId": "bbbbbbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb", "weight": 250 }

### CRUD : liste des profils
GET {{host}}/api/reputation/profiles

### CRUD : creer un profil (201, 409 si developerId existe deja)
POST {{host}}/api/reputation/profiles
Content-Type: application/json

{ "developerId": "44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444", "displayName": "nouveau.dev", "skills": ["python"] }

### CRUD : lire un profil
GET {{host}}/api/reputation/profiles/1

### CRUD : modifier un profil
PUT {{host}}/api/reputation/profiles/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "developerId": "{{dev}}", "displayName": "amine.dev", "skills": ["java", "spring", "docker"] }

### CRUD : supprimer un profil (204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/reputation/profiles/2

### Association : attribuer un badge manuellement
POST {{host}}/api/developers/{{dev}}/badges
Content-Type: application/json

{ "code": "MENTOR", "label": "Aide la communaute" }

### Association : historique des evenements
GET {{host}}/api/developers/{{dev}}/events

### Quelle instance repond ? (8086 ou 8096)
GET {{host}}/api/reputation/instance

### Actuator
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
###
GET {{host}}/actuator/info
###
GET {{host}}/actuator/metrics/http.server.requests
###
GET {{host}}/actuator/loggers/tn.arene.reputation
